    {
      "image_path": "../../../transcripts/mineru/neural-network-methods-nlp/parts/part-001-pages-001-200/images/69f3376f187cd3e4dd0625fdf6bdd73e6a19049577d88aae84af90c589573853.jpg",
      "figure_id": "13.2",
      "caption_text": "Figure 13.2: 1D convolution+pooling over the sentence “the quick brown fox jumped over the lazy dog.” This is a narrow convolution (no padding is added to the sentence) with a window size of 3. Each word is translated to a 2-dim embedding vector (not shown). The embedding vectors are then concatenated, resulting in 6-dim window representations. Each of the seven windows is transferred through a $6 \\times 3$ filter (linear transformation followed by element-wise tanh), resulting in seven 3-dimensional filtered representations. Then, a max-pooling operation is applied, taking the max over each dimension, resulting in a final 3-dimensional pooled vector.",
      "caption_body_text": null,
      "status": "transcript-adjacent",
